+- Public validation repository's run record was committed separately at `67cc450b8a491a0e6b0595aa2ceb8ad2078820cd`.
+- Mission 81/original Metal, Mission 82, and unrelated worktrees were not modified.
+
+## Rights-safe CI result
+
+The CoopDX iOS source and previous Metal repository have no identified root license grant. No full source mirror was published and no code from the earlier Metal repository was copied. To obtain useful Apple validation without publishing the complete game source, a public source-only repository was created:
+
+- Repository: [sm64coopdx-metal-build](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build)
+- Commit: `7640f3b926a8e69f08bca1c93b011f49db4839b2`
+- Contents: four generated MSL fixtures, Apple compiler workflow, README, MIT license, and gitignore. No CoopDX engine, ROM, proprietary assets, renderer backend implementation, or app binary.
+- Workflow: [run 45738609822](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build/actions/runs/45738609822) — **passed**.
+- Public validation repository current commit: `67cc450b8a491a0e6b0595aa2ceb8ad2078820cd` (README records the verified run and artifact).
+- Runner/toolchain: macOS 15.8.2 ARM64, Xcode 16.4 build 16F6, iPhoneOS SDK 18.5.
+- Apple `metal -c` compiled actual adapter-generated fixtures covering textureless, texture tile 0, texture tile 1, and two-cycle fog/light-map/world color flags.
+- `.air` artifact: [download](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build/actions/runs/45738609822/artifacts/15080650158); 22,327 bytes; archive SHA-256 `e361ea24ccacb3df36d2a9fcde15cb29a82599e92fd7a083c56a1056aa558133`.
+- The artifact was downloaded and extracted; all four `.air` hashes matched the CI `SHA256SUMS.txt`.
+
+This proves only that Apple's compiler accepts these shader fixtures. It does not validate the Objective-C Metal backend, SDL integration, complete iOS app, linking, pipeline creation, GPU execution, or gameplay rendering.
+
+## Full app workflow blocker
+
+Private patch overlay: [sm64coopdx-metal-integration](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-integration). The latest full-project workflow, [run 45738244093](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-integration/actions/runs/45738244093), failed before runner allocation. The host job had zero steps; the iOS job was skipped. GitHub's annotation reports: “The job was not started because recent account payments have failed or your spending limit needs to be increased.” This is an account-level infrastructure block, not a source/compiler error. No billing or spending-limit changes were attempted. Do not repeat runs until the account-side block is cleared.
