+# Mission 06 Progress — Zero-Dollar Metal
+
+## Current disposition
+
+**Partial.** The rights-safe public Apple harness has compiled and linked the Metal backend components against Apple's iPhoneOS SDK and a stub CoopDX contract. The complete CoopDX application has not been Apple-compiled or linked, no IPA exists, and there is no iPhone result.
+
+## Repositories and checkpoints
+
+- Integration source: `/home/larry/Projects/sm64coopdx-metal`
+- Integration branch: `mission-03-04-metal-first-light-parity`
+- Latest local integration source checkpoint: `297c6075` (`Make Metal object cache ARC-safe`); current branch HEAD is `712b6edc` (documentation checkpoint). This branch has only the `upstream` remote; do not push it to upstream.
+- Private overlay: `/home/larry/Projects/sm64coopdx-metal-overlay`, local commit `a67c956` contains the Apple SDK and ARC fixes and materializes the validated source tree. It is one commit ahead of its private GitHub branch; it was not pushed because doing so would trigger the private Actions workflow while the billing restriction remains.
+- Public, source-only component harness: [LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build)
+- Latest public harness commit: `0c426ac76bd3a594f2aa47221e51c257164b80dd` (`Include the linked ARM64 Metal harness in CI artifacts`).
+- Verification run for corrected artifact path: [45746850842](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build/actions/runs/45746850842) — passed.
+- Artifact: [iphoneos-metal-components-0c426ac76bd3a594f2aa47221e51c257164b80dd](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build/actions/runs/45746850842/artifacts/15082744213), 1,455,487 bytes, 30-day retention. Every downloaded file matched `SHA256SUMS.txt`; the ARM64 test dylib is 2,020,720 bytes, SHA-256 `68d432761dac1ea880f5722fed2a18b496b1dd5fc99d987236ac879bad9bb6f9`.
+- The previous run [45746603843](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build/actions/runs/45746603843) passed its build steps, but its artifact omitted the test dylib due to an incorrect upload path. Commit `0c426ac` fixed the path; the successful next run includes and verifies the dylib.
+
+## Evidence achieved
+
+Earlier public run [45738609822](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build/actions/runs/45738609822) compiled four adapter-generated MSL fixtures with Apple's Metal compiler (Xcode 16.4 build 16F6, macOS 15.8.2 ARM64, iPhoneOS SDK 18.5).
+
+On public run `45746850842`, the standard macOS ARM64 runner successfully:
+
+- Built pinned official SDL 2.32.10 as an iPhoneOS ARM64 static library.
+- Compiled the Objective-C Metal backend, C adapter, and SDL Metal layer bridge against the iPhoneOS SDK.
+- Linked a stub-contract test dylib against Apple's frameworks and SDL2.
+- Generated and compiled eight representative MSL variants (including alpha, DynOS/custom material, HUD alpha, character texture replacement, runtime texture rebind, and two-cycle fog/light-map).
+- Ran SDL Metal layer lifecycle tests, including the sanitizer invocation.
+
+This validates those independently published components and their stub contract only. The test dylib is a linked harness, not the game application. It does not establish ABI compatibility with the complete game, full application linking, GPU execution, rendering parity, or LiveContainer behavior.
+
+## Local validation
+
+On the integration tree, these passed after the Apple-diagnostic fixes:
+
+- `make -j2`
+- `tests/run_gfx_metal_coopdx_shader_test.sh`
+- `SANITIZE=1 CC=clang tests/run_gfx_metal_coopdx_shader_test.sh`
+- `tests/run_gfx_sdl_metal_layer_test.sh`
+- `SANITIZE=1 CC=clang tests/run_gfx_sdl_metal_layer_test.sh`
+- `git diff --check`
+
+The Apple diagnostics found and corrected the Metal sampler enum spelling, Objective-C ARC bridging, scissor-rectangle construction, Objective-C `id` shadowing by a texture-ID local, and test-link dependencies for SDL's iOS static library. The Metal object cache now releases ARC-owned pipeline references by assigning `nil`, rather than clearing Objective-C objects with `memset`.
+
+The public harness originally tried to fetch the private overlay with a token on a public runner. That workflow was deleted in commit `b5b682b`; it was not dispatched. The public workflow now builds only independently authored, permitted components.
+
+## Full-app routes checked
+
+- The GitHub API reports `license: null` for `LeoManrique/sm64coopdx-ios`, `coop-deluxe/sm64coopdx`, and `LawrenceBanes/sm64ios-metal` (checked 2026-11-26 UTC). The source trees have no established root license grant. A complete public mirror or upload to a public build runner is not justified.
+- Private integration Actions were rejected before runner allocation with the exact annotation “The job was not started because recent account payments have failed or your spending limit needs to be increased” (run `45738244093`). The iOS job was skipped and both jobs had zero steps. No paid runner, trial, billing change, or bypass was used.
+- This execution host is Linux x86_64 with no `xcodebuild` or `xcrun`. Tailscale currently lists this Linux host and the iPhone; there is no reachable Mac build host.
+- The user-owned local ROM remains local and was not copied to public CI.
+
+Therefore Mission 06's primary target (complete Apple app build and private IPA) remains blocked by the currently available, legitimate zero-cost build routes. The public component artifact is not an IPA and must not be presented as one.
+
+## Next actions
+
+1. The component artifact is downloaded and its checksum manifest is verified; retain this as component-only evidence.
+2. Continue source-only checks that do not expose the unlicensed full engine or consume paid runners. A complete build needs an already-authorized Apple host and a lawful source route; do not send the private source through public Actions.
+3. If a Mac becomes available, run the private overlay build, package and validate the IPA locally, then publish only to the private release. Keep ROM and game data local.
+
+## Evidence labels
+
+- **Host tested:** portable Linux build and tests listed above.
+- **Apple component-compiled/linked:** the public harness workflow; stub interfaces only.
+- **Full iPhoneOS app compiled/linked:** not verified.
+- **IPA packaged/validated:** not produced.
+- **Device verified:** not tested.
